---
import Page from '../../../layouts/Page.astro';

---

<Page
	title="Free stand test logger: track orthostatic heart rate over time"
	description="A free Google Sheets template for logging NASA lean test and active stand test results over time. Record heart rate at baseline, 2, 5, and 10 minutes standing. Track your orthostatic response."
>
			<div class="page-header">
				<a href="/tools/" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
				<h1>Stand test logger</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">Free Google Sheets template for tracking orthostatic heart rate over time</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content">
				<p>If you are using the NASA lean test or a similar active stand test to monitor your orthostatic heart rate response, this Google Sheets logger gives you a structured way to record and track your results over time.</p>

				<p>The logger includes fields for heart rate at baseline (lying), then at 2, 5, and 10 minutes of standing, along with a date, any notes (such as hydration status, time of day, or how you felt), and automatic calculation of the heart rate rise at each interval.</p>

				<p>A single stand test result is useful but limited. Repeating the test over days and weeks gives you a much more reliable picture of your orthostatic response, and makes it easier to see whether an intervention (such as increased salt and fluid intake, compression, or medication) is making a measurable difference.</p>

				<p>This pairs well with the <a href="/tools/nasa-lean-test/">NASA lean test guide</a>, which walks you through the test step by step with an interactive timer. If you are just starting out, <a href="/testing/do-i-have-pots/">Do I have POTS?</a> explains what your results mean and how to take them to your GP.</p>

				<h2>How to use this template</h2>
				<p>Click the button below to open the template in Google Sheets. Because it is a shared template, you will not be able to edit it directly. To get your own editable copy, go to <strong>File → Make a copy</strong> in the Google Sheets menu. This saves a version to your own Google Drive that only you can see and edit. The original template is not affected.</p>
				<p>You do not need to share any data with anyone. Once you have made your copy, it is entirely private to you.</p>

				<a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1SXMyBUa9eyfv01wyk9arEziqeb8L7e245YT0A0PTZrc/edit?gid=0#gid=0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="cta-button">Open the stand test logger template →</a>
			</div>
</Page>

